igraph
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Grafi's optional native extension (the NIF in c_src/) is a bridge to the
igraph C library, https://igraph.org, which is licensed under the GNU General
Public License, version 2 or later (GPL-2.0-or-later). igraph is not included
in the Grafi source package.

* Building from source: when igraph >= 1.0 is installed, the NIF is compiled
  and dynamically linked against it on your machine. Without igraph, no NIF is
  built and Grafi runs in pure Elixir.

* Precompiled NIF artefacts (grafi-nif-*.tar.gz on the GitHub releases page,
  downloaded by default when Grafi is installed from Hex on a supported
  platform) statically link igraph 1.0.1. Each artefact combines Apache-2.0
  code (Grafi's NIF, the fine headers) with GPL code (igraph). Because the
  Apache License 2.0 is compatible with GPL version 3 but not version 2, each
  artefact is distributed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or
  later (GPL-3.0-or-later); see LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt. Every
  artefact also contains the GPL-3.0 and Apache-2.0 texts and igraph's
  licence files (grafi_nif.licenses/igraph). [Pending legal review; see
  RELEASING.md.]

  If you distribute software that includes a precompiled artefact (for
  example a `mix release`), the GPL-3.0-or-later applies to that artefact.
  To ship no GPL code, build without igraph (see the README, "The igraph NIF
  (optional)").

  The igraph build used for the artefacts leaves out GLPK, GraphML, OpenMP
  and Infomap, which Grafi does not use. It includes igraph's other vendored
  components (BLAS, LAPACK, ARPACK, mini-GMP, plfit, CXSparse, qhull and
  others), whose licences ship in the igraph source distribution (COPYING and
  vendor/); igraph's COPYING, AUTHORS, licence overview and the vendored
  licence files (CXSparse, f2c, PCG, qhull) are also in every artefact.

  Corresponding source for a precompiled artefact (also attached to each
  GitHub release):
    - igraph 1.0.1:
      https://github.com/igraph/igraph/releases/download/1.0.1/igraph-1.0.1.tar.gz
      (SHA-256 969f2d7d22f67e788d8638c9a8c96615f50d7819c08978b3ef4a787bb6daa96c,
      as in .github/igraph.env)
    - Grafi, at the git tag of the release the artefact is attached to:
      https://github.com/nyo16/grafi
    - The exact build: .github/scripts/ and .github/workflows/release.yml at
      that tag.
